### Local IDP backend: run with --server.port=8081 (see README "Run locally").
### AgentCore Runtime requires session ids of at least 33 characters, so the
### examples use ids of that length even locally.
@host = http://localhost:8081
@session = idp-session-00000000000000000000001

### Health check (AgentCore /ping contract)
GET {{host}}/ping

### List available specialist agents
GET {{host}}/api/agents

### Lawyer reviews an unsigned lease (text) via the AgentCore contract endpoint.
### Expect the 'legal-unsigned' ALERT.
POST {{host}}/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: {{session}}

{
  "agentType": "LAWYER",
  "question": "Is this lease tenant-friendly, and is it signed?",
  "mimeType": "text/plain",
  "content": "RESIDENTIAL LEASE AGREEMENT\nLandlord: Example Properties LLC\nTenant: Jane Doe\nTerm: 12 months from 2026-07-01\nRent: $2,100 per month\nTenant is liable for all damages without limit.\nLandlord may enter the premises at any time without notice.\nLandlord signature: ____________\nTenant signature: ____________"
}

### Mortgage advisor checks completeness. Expect the 'mortgage-missing-income' ALERT.
POST {{host}}/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: {{session}}

{
  "agentType": "MORTGAGE",
  "question": "Is this application complete for underwriting?",
  "mimeType": "text/plain",
  "content": "MORTGAGE APPLICATION\nApplicant: John Smith\nLoan amount: $420,000\nProperty value: $500,000\nMonthly debts: $3,400\nGross monthly income: (not provided)\nEmployment verification: pending"
}

### Auto-classify (no agentType) and answer a question
POST {{host}}/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: {{session}}

{
  "question": "What kind of document is this, what is due, and when?",
  "mimeType": "text/plain",
  "content": "CITY UTILITIES\nAccount: 99-1234\nBilling period: 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-31\nAmount due: $142.18\nDue date: 2026-06-20\nLate fee: $15.00 after due date"
}

### Interactive file upload: choose agent + attach a file (multipart)
# Most editors support file refs in .http files; otherwise use the curl form in the README.
POST {{host}}/api/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----idp

------idp
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="agentType"

LAWYER
------idp
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="question"

Is this lease signed?
------idp
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="lease-agreement.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./samples/lease-agreement.pdf
------idp--

### Prometheus metrics (idp.documents.processed, idp.extraction.confidence, idp.alerts.sent)
GET {{host}}/actuator/prometheus
